.TH FREECSIM 1 2026-11-17 "FreeCUPL 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
freecsim \- CSIM compatible PLD simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freecsim
.RI [ \-flags ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ library ]
.RI [ device ]
.IR file [ .si ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freecsim
applies the test vectors of
.IB file .si
to the design compiled by
.BR freecupl (1)
into the absolute file
.IB file .abs\fR,
writes the waveform file
.IB file .wo
and, on request, the listing
.IB file .so
and test vectors appended to the JEDEC file.
Its command line follows the simulator of WinCUPL 5.0a.
.PP
Each input name is tried in lower case first, then in upper case.
.IR device ,
when given, must be the device of the absolute file.
.I library
is accepted and ignored.
.PP
The same simulation is run by
.BR "freecupl \-s" .
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-l
Write the listing
.IB file .so\fR.
.TP
.B \-v
Also show the listing on the terminal.
.TP
.B \-j
Append the test vectors to the JEDEC file named after the design's
.B Name
header item, or
.IB file .jed
with
.BR \-n .
.TP
.B \-n
See
.BR \-j .
.TP
.B \-u
The next positional argument is the library (ignored).
.TP
.B \-w \-d
Accepted; no effect.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-compat\-refdefect
Reproduce WinCUPL 5.0a's simulator exactly, including its bugs.
.TP
.B \-fix
Correct the bugs: the default.
.TP
.B \-simlatch
Simulate latched outputs and registered or latched inputs (timing not
verified); by default they show X.
.TP
.BI \-fuses " FILE.jed"
Simulate the fuse map of
.I FILE.jed
instead of the one in the absolute file.
.TP
.B \-info
Print the design's signals (name, pin, polarity, role) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
When set to a number of seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC, that time is
written as the creation date in the listing instead of the current time.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the simulation ran without errors; 1 when a file could not be
read, on an invalid flag, or when the simulation reported errors (for
example an expected value that differs,
.BR [0019sa] ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR freecupl (1);
docs/USERGUIDE.txt, docs/SIMFMT.txt and docs/BUGS.txt in the FreeCUPL
distribution.
